The Harlequins are the builders of the Strider and the organizers of the pilgrimage.

The [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]], the strider at [[Geography/Calaria/Ragged Roost|Ragged Roost]], is their work: a platform on eight legs with buildings on top.

At a pilgrimage the Harlequins wear red-and-green pinstriped shirts, bell-capped masks whose shadow hides the line of the neck, and gloves. They take invitations at the head of the line and hand out plain white masks to guests. Others walk the street with platters of champagne and hors d'oeuvres, run the attractions, or mop the arena floor after a fight.

They run games along the main street and the paths out of town: a fortune teller's booth, an association game on the fairy-ring path, a barker before a rainbow prism with a key at its center, and a table of dice. Winning a game pays a hint about a [[Phenomena/Keystone|keystone]].

Once the guests are aboard, a Harlequin such as [[Org/The Harlequins/People/Chuck|Chuck]] is assigned as servant to each berth, dressed more richly than the rest and carrying a scepter, and given whatever name its guests choose. The Harlequins also keep orts, the least of the devils, as laborers, walking them on leashes through the town and up onto the strider.

The town the Harlequins keep at the front of the strider has its own [[Org/The Harlequins/Harlequin Town|library and clock tower]], and [[Org/The Harlequins/People/Ocelith|Ocelith]] is its curator.
